+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up, and `/account` support passkeys (WebAuthn) alongside passwords:
+
+- **Sign in** offers passkeys in the username field's autofill and with a "Sign in with a passkey" button. After a password sign-in, supporting browsers can silently create a passkey (Conditional Create).
+- **Sign up** suggests creating a passkey once the account exists.
+- **Account settings** list, rename, create, and delete passkeys, and edit the display name. Sensitive changes require re-verification with a passkey or password if the last sign-in was more than 5 minutes ago.
+
+Passwords are still checked by the upstream account service; the app proxies those calls through `/api/auth/*` so it can keep a session. Passkey credentials are verified with [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/) and stored in `.data/auth.json` (override with `AUTH_DATA_FILE`). Passkeys only work on the hostnames listed in `src/lib/auth/config.ts` (override with a comma-separated `PASSKEY_RP_IDS`), over HTTPS or on `http://localhost`.
